  "id": "theoretical-construct",
  "term": "theoretical construct",
  "definition": "A theoretical construct is a concept within a theory that leads to predictions about what effects should be found in research. In psychology, it is considered empirically adequate when the effect the theory predicts is sufficiently similar to the effect actually observed.",
